<section xml:id="section-partial-sums-and-infinite-series" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    Partial Sums and Infinite Series
  </title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      We begin by developing a notion of convergence and divergence for series of real numbers. These ideas build directly on the convergence and divergence of sequences of real numbers. In fact, a series converges/diverges if and only if an associated sequence of real numbers (although <em> not </em> the sequence of terms) does.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="./subsection-infinitely-iterated-sums.ptx"/>

